  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nPotential for patchy frost Monday night across the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nStrong Canadian high pressure returns to the region Monday \nnight. With mostly clear skies amd light winds during the \novernight hours promoting favorable radiational cooling \nconditions. This likely will result in possible patchy frost. \nThis should mainly be limited to Northern regions with better \nchances in low lying areas.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nA coastal low could impact at least Downeast Maine late this\nweek.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA piece of energy currently located over the Bahamas will slowly\nslide northward, along the east coast, through the coming days. \nBy midweek, it will combine with a mid-level low tracking \neastward across the mid-Atlantic and begin to consolidate as a \nsurface low offshore.\n\nTiming and track of the system remains uncertain at this time.\nWith strong subtropical ridging to the East, the speed and track\nof the low will depend on the placement and subsequent\ndegradation of the strong Canadian high over Eastern Canada\nthrough the start of the weekend. Regardless of timing, the\ngreatest chance for any impacts will be over Coastal Downeast.",
